Now I understand the pattern. Each provider branch does Agent::new(Provider).with_model_config(model_config), and later .with_model(&self.model) is called. Since model_config already carries the model id (via configured_for), the migration is:

• Agent::new(Provider).with_model_config(cfg) → `Agent::from_provider(Provider, cfg)`
• Remove .with_model(...) calls since the model id now comes from the config.

